d on insertions of short and long interpersed elements: hippopotamuses are the closest extant relatives of whales</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci USA</source><year>1999</year><volume>96</volume><fpage>10261</fpage><lpage>10266</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10468596</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1073/pnas.96.18.10261</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Murphy</surname><given-names>WJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Eizirik</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>O'Brien</surname><given-names>SJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Madsen</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Scally</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Douady</surname><given-names>CJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Teeling</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Ryder</surname><given-names>OA</given-names></name><name><surname>Stanhope</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>de Jong</surname><given-names>WW</given-names></name><name><surname>Springer</surname><given-names>MS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Resolution of the early placental mammal radiation using Bayesian phylogenetics</article-title><source>Science</source><year>2001</year><volume>294</volume><fpage>2348</fpage><lpage>2351</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11743200</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1126/science.1067179</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Waddell</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Kishino</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Ota</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A phylogenetic foundation for comparative mammalian genomics</article-title><source>Genome Inform</source><year>2001</year><volume>12</volume><fpag