tp://www.science.smith.edu/departments/Biology/VHAYSSEN/msi/pdf/i0076-3519-527-01-0001.pdf"/><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.2307/3504117</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Best</surname><given-names>RC</given-names></name><name><surname>Silva</surname><given-names>VMF</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Inia geoffrensis</article-title><source>Mammalian Species No 426</source><year>1993</year><publisher-name>American Society of Mammologists</publisher-name><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>8</lpage><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.science.smith.edu/departments/Biology/VHAYSSEN/msi/pdf/i0076-3519-426-01-0001.pdf"/></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Best</surname><given-names>RC</given-names></name><name><surname>da Silva</surname><given-names>VMF</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Preliminary analysis of reproductive parameters of the boutu, Inia geoffrensis, and the tucuxi, Sotalia fluviatilis, in the Amazon River system</article-title><source>Rep Int Whal Commn, (Special Issue 6)</source><year>1984</year><fpage>361</fpage><lpage>369</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hamilton</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Caballero</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Collins</surname><given-names>AG</given-names></name><name><surname>Brownell</surname><given-names>RL</given-names><suffix>Jr</suffix></name></person-group><article-title>Evolution of river dolphins</article-title><source>Proc R Soc Lond B Biol Sci</source><year>2001</year><volume>268</volume><fpage>549</fpage><lpage>556</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1098/rspb.2000.1385</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-gr